From: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Nov 2025 11:27:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: initialize MT7990 band-1 RRO ring

MT7990, like MT7992, uses RRO band 1.  The current condition handles only
MT7992, so MT7990 falls into the MT7996-specific branch and allocates its
band-0 TX-free queue a second time instead.  Apart from leaving band-1 RRO
uninitialized, the duplicate allocation replaces the queue backing memory
after WED has already configured the TX-free ring.

Use the non-MT7996 condition from MediaTek's prerequisite MT7990 WED/RRO
patch.  This changes only MT7990: MT7992 keeps its existing band-1 RRO
setup and MT7996 keeps its TX-free branch.

This is adapted from MediaTek's MT7990 WED/RRO configuration patch.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0048-mtk-mt76-mt7996-add-configuration-to-suppot-wed-and-.patch
Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/dma.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/dma.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/dma.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -913,7 +913,7 @@ int mt7996_dma_init(struct mt7996_dev *d
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		if (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76)) {
+		if (!is_mt7996(&dev->mt76)) {
 			dev->mt76.q_rx[MT_RXQ_RRO_BAND1].flags =
 				MT_WED_RRO_Q_DATA(1) | MT_QFLAG_WED_RRO_EN;
 			if (mtk_wed_device_active(wed) &&
